# UI Foundations — Cline Rules

## Project

Token-first, Figma-aligned design system. Figma is a design-authoring projection of the UIF token model; durable architecture and contracts live in UIF-VLT.

## Token Architecture (4 layers)

| Layer | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Core (Primitives) | Raw values: spacing, radii, borders, typography |
| Appearance Modes | Light/dark color palettes |
| Semantics (Roles) | Intent-based: `--color-text-default`, `--color-fill-surface` |
| Components (UI) | Component-specific: `--button-solid-border-color-default` |

Rules: Components reference only Semantic or Core. Never hardcode values.

## Class Naming (Foundation-013)

- Root: `.component` (bare name)
- Parts: `.component-part` (hyphen-compound)
- Variants: `.component.variant` (multi-class)
- States: `.is-state` prefix
- NO double-underscores (`__`)
- NO BEM modifiers (`--`)
- NO namespace prefixes

## CSS Conventions

- Always wrap in `@layer components { }`
- Use logical properties: `inline-size`, `block-size`, not `width`, `height`
- Use `var(--token-name)` for all values — never hardcode
- States: both pseudo-classes (`:hover`) and fallback classes (`.is-hover`)
- Reuse existing patterns: icon-only buttons use `.uif-button.ghost` + `.uif-icon`

## Token Naming

`--component-variant-part-property-state`

Examples:
- `--button-solid-container-background-hover`
- `--uif-calendar-cell-text-color-disabled`

States always last: `default`, `hover`, `active`, `focus`, `disabled`

## Component Integration (10 Surfaces)

Every component needs ALL of these:

1. CSS pattern: `src/ui/patterns/<name>.css`
2. CSS import: `src/ui/index.css`
3. React wrapper: `src/react/<name>.js`
4. React export: `src/react/index.js`
5. Nunjucks macro: `site/_includes/macros/ui.njk`
6. Playground renderer: `site/assets/playground/renderers.js`
7. Docs page: `site/patterns/<name>.md`
8. Playground page: `site/patterns/<name>-playground.md`
9. Code Connect: `schemas/web-<name>.figma.ts`
10. Token definitions: `figma/exports/Components (UI).tokens.json`

## MCP Tools Available

Use the ui-foundations MCP server for project queries:
- `search_foundations` — full-text search across all docs
- `get_component` — component details
- `get_token` — token lookup
- `get_pattern` — CSS pattern info
- `get_rule` — governance rule details
- `validate_token_name` — check if a token name is valid
- `diagnose_drift` — check Figma/CSS alignment

## Commands

```bash
npm run build          # Full build
npm run lint           # JS lint
npm run test:unit      # Unit tests
npm run smoke:check    # Dist artifact verification
npm run tokens:generate # Regenerate CSS from Figma exports
```

## Key Files

| Surface | Path |
|---|---|
| CSS patterns | `src/ui/patterns/*.css` |
| React wrappers | `src/react/*.js` |
| Nunjucks macros | `site/_includes/macros/ui.njk` |
| Playground renderers | `site/assets/playground/renderers.js` |
| Token exports | `figma/exports/*.tokens.json` |
| Docs pages | `site/patterns/*.md` |

## Rules

- Never invent token names. Use `get_token` to verify.
- Never use `width`/`height` — use `inline-size`/`block-size`.
- Never hardcode colors, spacing, or typography values.
- Always run `npm run lint && npm run test:unit` after changes.
- Keep Brand and Appearance orthogonal via `data-brand` and `data-mode`.
